- timestamp: '2026-08-06T00:00:00+00:00'
  curator: issue_213_residual_triage
  action: FLAGGED_NEEDS_EXPERT
  changes: Class-level label, not a substance. No ontology carries a bare 'sugars'
    term, and grounding to a specific sugar or to MeSH 'Carbohydrates' would over-
    or under-specify. Needs a granularity decision. Searched CHEBI, NCIT, FOODON,
    ENVO, MeSH, BTO and UBERON by label and synonym with normalisation, plus exact
    queries across all of live OLS4.
  previous_status: UNMAPPED
  new_status: NEEDS_EXPERT
  llm_assisted: true
- timestamp: '2026-08-06T00:00:00+00:00'
  curator: edison_literature_identity
  action: ANNOTATED
  changes: 'Edison LITERATURE (PaperQA3) identity research; report at research/ingredients/Sugars-edison-literature.md
    (local artifact — research/ is gitignored, so the findings are quoted here rather
    than linked). Report verdict: ## Executive recommendation — **Retain `UNMAPPED`.**
    “Sugars” is an underspecified plural **chemical/component-family label**, not
    a single chemical, hydrate, salt, buffer, extract, or fixed commercial formulation.
    It therefore has no defensible unique molecular formula, charge, hydrate state,
    CAS Registry Number, or composition. No identity-level SSSOM row should be created
    from the available evi No ontology CURIE was proposed. Recorded as provenance
    only — no grounding applied from this run. Edison''s recommendations are deliberately
    conservative, and a plausible identifier promoted by a mechanism that never decided
    anything is what #203 and #263 exist to undo. Any CURIE above is a curator''s
    to accept or reject.'
  llm_assisted: true
- timestamp: '2026-08-15T00:00:00+00:00'
  curator: decompose_py_media_and_ground_categories
  action: GROUNDED_TO_CHEBI_CLASS
  previous_status: NEEDS_EXPERT
  new_status: MAPPED
  changes: 'UNMAPPED_0663 -> kgmicrobe.compound:sugars; ontology_id CHEBI:16646 (NARROW_MATCH).
    Grounded to the ChEBI class CHEBI:16646 (''carbohydrate''): the label names a
    CATEGORY, and a ChEBI class is what a category should map to — the mirror image
    of #322, where records naming specific substances were wrongly on class terms.
    NARROW_MATCH because sugars are a proper subset of carbohydrates: ChEBI carries
    no `sugar` synonym on CHEBI:16646, so this is a real subclass relation and not
    a naming variant. Rule B1 then requires a sibling registry row, so the record
    takes a kgmicrobe.compound mint.'
  llm_assisted: false
- timestamp: '2026-08-15T00:00:00+00:00'
  curator: move_mapped_out_of_unmapped_collection
  action: MOVED_TO_MAPPED_COLLECTION
  changes: Moved from unmapped_ingredients.yaml to mapped_ingredients.yaml (#370).
    The record was already MAPPED; it had been promoted in place by a path that does
    not move between collections, and reconcile_sssom reads only the mapped collection
    — so its mapping was curated but unpublished.
  llm_assisted: false
